---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BotanicalScrollReveal from "@components/BotanicalScrollReveal.astro";
const lastUpdated = "June 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Moka Bio"
  description="How Moka Bio collects, uses, and protects your personal information. Covers GDPR and CCPA."
>
  <div class="legal-page">
    <BotanicalScrollReveal src="/assets/about-botanicals/botanical-line-01.png" revealStart={-0.15} revealRange={0.36} tone="strong" class="privacy-botanical-focus" />
    <div class="legal-header">
      <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-freshgreen/25 to-transparent"></div>
      <p class="legal-kicker">LEGAL</p>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-body">

      <div class="legal-notice">
        <p class="legal-notice-heading">Scope of This Policy</p>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy applies exclusively to personal information collected through
          the <strong>moka.bio</strong> website (the "Site"). It does not govern the processing
          of personal data collected in connection with commercial service agreements or research
          partnerships, which are addressed separately in individual data processing agreements
          executed with each client or partner.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. Who We Are / Data Controller</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Moka Bio, Inc.</strong> is a corporation organized under the laws of the
          State of Delaware, United States of America ("Moka Bio", "we", "us", "our").
          Moka Bio is the data controller responsible for the personal information described
          in this Policy.
        </p>
        <p>
          For data protection inquiries, contact us at:
          <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3>Information you provide directly</h3>
        <p>When you submit the contact form on our Site, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your full name</li>
          <li>Your professional email address</li>
          <li>Your phone number (optional)</li>
          <li>Your organization or company (if provided)</li>
          <li>The content of your message</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This information is used solely to respond to your inquiry and to evaluate potential
          business opportunities. We do not use it for any marketing, profiling, or automated
          decision-making.
        </p>

        <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
        <p>
          When you visit the Site, we automatically collect certain technical and usage data
          through <strong>Google Analytics (GA4)</strong>, including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pages visited and navigation path</li>
          <li>Time spent on each page</li>
          <li>Device type, browser, and operating system</li>
          <li>General geographic location (country and city level)</li>
          <li>Referral source (how you arrived at the Site)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Google Analytics uses IP anonymization by default. No personally identifiable
          information is transmitted to Google in connection with analytics. We do not
          combine analytics data with any personal information you provide through forms.
        </p>

        <h3>Information we do not collect</h3>
        <p>We do not collect sensitive personal data such as health information, financial
        data, biometric data, racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious beliefs,
        or trade union membership through this Site.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. Legal Bases for Processing (GDPR)</h2>
        <p>
          For users in the European Economic Area (EEA) and United Kingdom (UK), we process
          your personal data under the following legal bases:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Legitimate Interests (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR)</strong> — Processing contact
            form submissions to evaluate and respond to business inquiries is necessary for
            our legitimate interests in operating a business, and does not override your rights
            and freedoms given the limited and expected nature of such processing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legitimate Interests (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR)</strong> — Collecting anonymized
            website analytics to understand and improve our Site's content and performance,
            where the minimal privacy impact does not outweigh our business interests.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR)</strong> — Where we rely on consent (e.g.,
            for any optional communications), you may withdraw it at any time by contacting
            us at <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>, without affecting the
            lawfulness of processing prior to withdrawal.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. How We Use Your Data</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact form submissions</strong> — to respond to your message, follow up on your inquiry, and evaluate whether a business relationship may be relevant.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics data</strong> — to understand how visitors interact with the Site, improve content and user experience, and inform our product and marketing strategy. We never sell this data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not use your personal data for automated decision-making, profiling, behavioral
          advertising, or any purpose incompatible with those stated above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Contact form data</strong> is retained for up to 36 months from the date of
          submission, or for as long as necessary to pursue or maintain a business relationship,
          whichever is longer. After this period, data is securely deleted unless a legal
          obligation requires longer retention.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Analytics data</strong> is retained in Google Analytics for 14 months in
          line with Google's default settings, after which it is automatically deleted from
          Google's systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          Retention periods may be extended where required by applicable law, regulatory
          obligation, or the legitimate resolution of a dispute.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to any third party.
          We may share data only in the following limited circumstances:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Google LLC</strong> — for analytics services under our agreement with
            Google, governed by <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>
            and Google's Data Processing Amendment.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Email and productivity infrastructure</strong> — we use standard commercial
            email and productivity services to manage correspondence. These providers act as
            data processors and are bound by appropriate contractual data protection obligations.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legal authorities</strong> — where disclosure is required by applicable
            law, court order, or governmental authority, or where necessary to protect the
            rights, property, or safety of Moka Bio, its clients, or the public.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Business transfers</strong> — in connection with a merger, acquisition,
            or sale of all or substantially all of Moka Bio's assets, your data may be
            transferred to the acquiring entity subject to equivalent privacy protections.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>7. International Data Transfers</h2>
        <p>
          Moka Bio is incorporated in the United States and may operate across multiple jurisdictions. Personal data submitted through the Site may be stored and processed on
          servers located in the United States or other countries outside your country of
          residence.
        </p>
        <p>
          For transfers of personal data from the EEA or UK to countries not recognized as
          providing an adequate level of data protection, we apply appropriate safeguards in
          accordance with GDPR Chapter V, which may include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) approved by the European Commission</li>
          <li>UK International Data Transfer Agreements (IDTAs) where applicable</li>
          <li>Binding Corporate Rules or other approved transfer mechanisms</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You may request a copy of the specific safeguards applicable to your data transfer
          by contacting us at <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Our Site uses a minimal set of cookies necessary for analytics. We do not use
          advertising, tracking, remarketing, or third-party social media cookies.
        </p>
        <div class="legal-table-wrap">
          <table class="legal-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Cookie</th>
                <th>Provider</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Expires</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>_ga</td>
                <td>Google Analytics</td>
                <td>Distinguishes unique users (anonymized)</td>
                <td>2 years</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>_ga_*</td>
                <td>Google Analytics</td>
                <td>Maintains session state for analytics</td>
                <td>2 years</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          You can opt out of Google Analytics tracking at any time using the
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
          You can also manage cookies through your browser settings; however, disabling cookies
          may affect your experience of the Site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>9. Your Rights — EEA and UK Users (GDPR / UK GDPR)</h2>
        <p>
          If you are located in the European Economic Area or United Kingdom, you have the
          following rights under the GDPR and UK GDPR:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Right of Access (Art. 15)</strong> — Request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Rectification (Art. 16)</strong> — Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Erasure (Art. 17)</strong> — Request deletion of your personal data ("right to be forgotten"), subject to legal retention obligations.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Restriction (Art. 18)</strong> — Request that we restrict processing of your data in certain circumstances.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Data Portability (Art. 20)</strong> — Receive your data in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Object (Art. 21)</strong> — Object to processing based on legitimate interests. We will cease processing unless we demonstrate compelling legitimate grounds.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Withdraw Consent</strong> — Where processing is based on consent, withdraw it at any time without affecting prior processing.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Lodge a Complaint</strong> — File a complaint with your competent supervisory authority. In the EEA, you may contact your national data protection authority; in the UK, the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>.
          We will respond within 30 days (extendable to 60 days for complex requests).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>10. Your Rights — California Residents (CCPA / CPRA)</h2>
        <p>
          If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), as
          amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), grants you the following rights:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Right to Know</strong> — the categories and specific pieces of personal information we collect, use, disclose, and sell (we do not sell your data).</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Delete</strong> — request deletion of personal information we have collected from you, subject to certain exceptions.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Correct</strong> — request correction of inaccurate personal information.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Opt-Out of Sale/Sharing</strong> — we do not sell or share your personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Non-Discrimination</strong> — we will not discriminate against you for exercising your privacy rights.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise your CCPA rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>.
          We will respond within 45 days, extendable to 90 days where necessary.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>11. Additional Jurisdictional Rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your country of residence, additional data protection rights may apply
          to you under local law. Where mandatory local law grants you rights that are broader
          than those described in this Policy, those rights will apply to the extent required.
          To exercise any applicable rights, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>12. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          We implement appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect your personal
          data against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. These measures
          include access controls, encryption in transit, and limited personnel access to personal data.
        </p>
        <p>
          No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure. While we take
          commercially reasonable steps to protect your data, we cannot guarantee absolute security.
          In the event of a personal data breach that is likely to result in a risk to your rights
          and freedoms, we will notify the relevant supervisory authorities and, where required,
          affected individuals, in accordance with applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>13. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The Site is directed exclusively at business professionals and is not intended for
          individuals under the age of 16 (or the applicable age of digital consent in your
          jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personal data from minors. If you believe
          we have inadvertently collected information from a minor, please contact us immediately
          at <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a> and we will take steps to
          delete it promptly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>14. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our
          practices, technology, legal requirements, or other factors. When we do, we will
          update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page.
        </p>
        <p>
          For material changes that significantly affect your rights or how we use your data,
          we will take reasonable steps to notify you (such as displaying a notice on the Site).
          Continued use of the Site after changes are posted constitutes your acceptance of
          the revised Policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>15. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions, requests, or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our data practices,
          contact us at:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Moka Bio, Inc.</strong><br />
          Delaware, United States of America<br />
          <a href="mailto:info@moka.bio">info@moka.bio</a>
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 13px; color: rgba(222,222,222,0.38);">
          We will acknowledge receipt of your request within 72 hours and respond substantively
          within the timeframes required by applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--charcoal-color);
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  .legal-header {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 10;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 5.5rem 1.5rem 3.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.06);
  }

  .legal-kicker {
    font-family: Roboto, sans-serif;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.46em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fresh-green-color);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--pure-color);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-family: Roboto, sans-serif;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.35);
  }

  /* ── Body ─────────────────────────────────────── */
  .legal-body {
    max-width: 1040px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 10;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 6rem;
  }

  /* ── Scope notice ─────────────────────────────── */
  .legal-notice {
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.82);
    padding: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(110, 191, 126, 0.30);
    background: rgba(19, 45, 37, 0.52);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .legal-notice::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 12% 0%, rgba(110, 191, 126, 0.10), transparent 40%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .legal-notice-heading {
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fresh-green-color);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .legal-notice p { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* ── Sections ─────────────────────────────────── */
  .legal-section {
    margin-bottom: 1.35rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.07);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.46);
    backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
  }

  .legal-section:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--pure-color);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(110, 191, 126, 0.10);
  }

  .legal-section h3 {
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.78);
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0.4rem;
  }

  .legal-section p {
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.62);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .legal-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .legal-section ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .legal-section li {
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.62);
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--fresh-green-color);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(110, 191, 126, 0.3);
    transition: border-color 200ms;
  }

  .legal-section a:hover { border-color: var(--fresh-green-color); }

  .legal-section strong {
    color: rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.88);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ── Table ───────────────────────────────────── */
  .legal-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.08);
  }

  .legal-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .legal-table th {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.5);
    background: rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.6);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.08);
  }

  .legal-table td {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    color: rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.62);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(222, 222, 222, 0.05);
  }

  .legal-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
</style>
